Hold each event once: Python's event cache is now the Rust event cache that the Rust sync handler and state resolution read, and Rust caches are evicted under `cache_autotuning` memory pressure. The `*getEvent*` cache no longer reports a memory gauge when `caches.track_memory_usage` is on. `experimental_features.rust_sync: on` no longer needs `rust_sync_allow_unshared_event_cache`.
